       ("People search the Outer Banks town by town", "<p>Nobody experiences the Outer Banks as one place, and nobody searches it that way either. A family set on Corolla is not comparison-shopping Hatteras. A couple planning a Manteo weekend, a surfer watching Kill Devil Hills, a bride pricing Duck wedding venues: each searches their town, their activity and their week. One generic page about the Outer Banks ranks for none of those searches. Town-level pages, activity pages and honest local detail are what Google can actually rank, and what a ready-to-book traveler actually clicks.</p>"),
